{"agent":"bg67","data":{"by":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"In `_withdraw_stale_wait`, the check `if globs is None or withheld:` prevents withdrawal when `withheld` is non-empty. However, the intent of the bug fix is to remove a stale wait when an update drops files, even if other files are withheld or requested. Specifically, if a user updates `--globs src/a.py` after previously requesting `--globs src/a.py,src/b.py`, `withheld` might contain files that are contested or withheld during the new update, causing `withheld` to be non-empty and prematurely returning. This leaves the stale wait record active, directly violating the intent of B-update-queue-wait-not-withdrawable where narrowing an update should clear the stale wait on dropped/absent globs.","digest":"1e7144047d75c8ac","family":"google","location":"ddflow/api/items/_edit.py:449","reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/items/_edit.py:449"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":5262,"diff_sha":"5a8bb41d29c7453528e513924d6f47e8987673ffc12706a609b5d67e8bc4ae2b","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B-update-queue-wait-not-withdrawable","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":1.2,"family":"google","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","output_digest":"339eecf42ee96694","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-update-queue-wait-not-withdrawable.critic.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261108T101621Z-47bdbfce.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"cb6f69a0194b3ebd2b4b7ede801bb19c945b069d","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/items/_edit.py":"100644 3971aebae38f8829b0290c6633188083274d5d88","ddflow/services/waiting.py":"100644 2c9a03bb8ebcb27009388091fc687c699d5ab043","tests/test_no_hold_and_wait.py":"100644 bee2717a539a26df68111a93ccdc3075defd563f"},"reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","reviewer_digest":"c7d1b7506be569ee","reviewer_families":["deepseek","google","xai"],"round":3,"rounds":3,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/api/items/_edit.py:449"],"tree_sha":"cb6f69a0194b+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"e23048272c3429cc850530c42","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":154257,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B-update-queue-wait-not-withdrawable","ts":"2026-11-08T10:19:36.779956Z"}
{"agent":"bg67","data":{"digest":"1e7144047d75c8ac","finding":1,"gate":"critic","location":"ddflow/api/items/_edit.py:449","probe":"REFUTED (same concern as round 1, already probed): a clean narrow ('update --globs src/a.py') has withheld=[] (no contested file in the new ask), so _withdraw_stale_wait's 'withheld' guard does NOT skip it -- that is the bug's defining path, pinned by test_a_narrowing_update_withdraws_a_stale_wait. A non-empty withheld only arises on a partial-accept WIDENING, where _waiting->register for the withheld glob REPLACES the prior lease.waiting record (latest event wins in State.waiting); probe test_a_new_withheld_ask_replaces_a_cancelled_wait_not_lingers_it asserts state.waiting[T1].globs == ['src/c.py'] after such an update, i.e. the still-wanted file, never the cancelled src/b.py. Both probes pass.","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/items/_edit.py:449","verdict":"refuted"},"id":"eca02b1f7d7f4ee3b77e00ebb","kind":"review.triaged","lamport":154278,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B-update-queue-wait-not-withdrawable","ts":"2026-11-08T10:23:18.103132Z"}
